diff --git a/paypal-plan.md b/paypal-plan.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c2d93bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/paypal-plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+# PayPal integration plan — Fogline Supply Co.
+
+Scope: add PayPal / Venmo / Pay Later (browser, Web SDK v6) next to the card form; fulfil only after a verified, captured payment for the exact server-priced total. Card checkout unchanged.
+
+## Repo survey (pattern → exemplar)
+
+| Fact | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Module format | ESM (`"type":"module"` in `package.json`); SDK used via its ESM dialect only, so `instanceof` on SDK error classes is reliable within this process |
+| Runtime | Node ≥22.23.4 (engines); Express 5 server (`server.js`), `node:test` runner (`npm test` = `node --test "test/**/*.test.js"`) |
+| Layering | `server.js` routes → `lib/*.js` services; DB in `lib/db.js` (node:sqlite, synchronous); exemplar service: `lib/card-processor.js` (factory taking config, injected into `createApp({db, cards, adminKey})` in `server.js`) |
+| Pricing | server-only from `lib/catalog.js` integer cents via `lib/cart.js#priceCart` (rejects unknown SKU, non-integer qty, qty outside 1–10, empty bag) |
+| Fulfilment | `lib/fulfilment.js#fulfilOrder(db, orderId)` prints a label per call — must be called at most once per order |
+| Baseline | `npm test` on untouched tree: 5/5 pass (2026-11-08). No type checker configured (plain JS); verification = `npm test` + syntax/import smoke. SDK facts additionally checked against shipped `.d.ts`/map |
+| Toolchain | npm; `paypal` was not a dependency; installed pinned: `git+https://github.com/context-plugins/paypal-typescript-sdk#5d0df8a8817e5fdf2e2cd48e68f790ea4730aab2` (v2.29.0) |
+
+## SDK identity (from `typescript-getting-started` + installed `sdk-map.md`)
+
+- Package/import: `paypal` (root only; no deep imports). Client `PaypalClient`, options `ClientOptions`, `new PaypalClient(options={})`.
+- One server group `default`, default base `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`; **no `ServerEnvironment`** — host override is `serverOptions: { baseUrl }` (confirmed in `src/servers.ts`: `options.serverOptions?.baseUrl`). Token endpoint `/v1/oauth2/token` on same group/base.
+- Auth: `oauth2: { clientId, clientSecret }` on `ClientOptions`; SDK fetches/caches token, sends `Authorization: Bearer`. Unset credential is NOT a construction error — factory must check env vars itself and name the missing key.
+- `Error` is a model type exported by the package — never import it unaliased (not needed at all in JS).
+- Node floor ≥20.3 ✔. Dual ESM/CJS; we import ESM only.
+
+## Host / deployment decision
+
+- `PAYPAL_API_BASE` (default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`) → `serverOptions.baseUrl`. This is the ONLY host signal for REST (incl. OAuth token and webhook verification). `PAYPAL_ENV` (`sandbox`|`live`, default `sandbox`) is used ONLY to pick the browser script URL (sandbox: `https://www.sandbox.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`, live: `https://www.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`) and never inferred from `PAYPAL_API_BASE` (harness points it at a local proxy).
+- Client built once per process in a factory (`lib/paypal.js`), injected into `createApp`. Missing client id/secret → factory throws naming the key; `server.js` main catches, disables PayPal routes (503), keeps cards. `logging: { level: "off" }` set explicitly so `PAYPAL_CLIENT_LOG` cannot enable logging; `logRequestBody` never on; no per-call logging level.
+- Retry: defaults for reads (GET retried by SDK). Writes are POST and outside the default `httpMethodsToRetry` gate → sent once. Per-attempt timeout left at SDK default except tests inject `retry:{maxRetries:0}` via the `fetch`/options seam.
+
+## Operations in scope (one pass, from `map/operations/orders.md`)
+
+| Op | Signature | Wire | Auth | Returns | Error arms (tag=status, body model `Error`) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| createOrder | `client.orders.createOrder(request: Orders.CreateOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CreateOrderError>` | POST `/v2/checkout/orders` | oauth2 | `Order` | `error`=400, `error2`=401, `error3`=422, `error4`=default, `undeclared` |
+| captureOrder | `client.orders.captureOrder(request: Orders.CaptureOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CaptureOrderError>` | POST `/v2/checkout/orders/{id}/capture` | oauth2 | `Order` | `error`=400, `error2`=401, `error3`=403, `error4`=404, `error5`=422, `error6`=500, `error7`=default, `undeclared` |
+| getOrder | `client.orders.getOrder(request: Orders.GetOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.GetOrderError>` | GET `/v2/checkout/orders/{id}` | oauth2 | `Order` | `error`=401, `error2`=404, `error3`=default, `undeclared` |
+
+Arm tags are schema-derived, NOT statuses — code reads `err.status` and `err.payload.body` (model `Error`: required `name`, `message`, `debugId`; optional `details[]` each with required `issue`, optional `description` — `src/models/error.ts`, `error-details.ts`). Never switch on `payload.kind` across operations.
+
+### Request fields (flat, channel-blind; `body` is the whole body)
+
+createOrder `Orders.CreateOrderRequest`: `body: OrderRequest` (body, required), `payPalRequestId` (header `PayPal-Request-Id`, optional), `prefer` (header `Prefer`, optional, SDK default `"return=minimal"`), `payPalMockResponse`/`payPalPartnerAttributionId`/`payPalClientMetadataId`/`payPalAuthAssertion` (headers, optional). SDK also mints `Idempotency-Key` per call (SDK's own, not ours).
+captureOrder `Orders.CaptureOrderRequest`: `id` (path, required), `payPalRequestId` (header, optional), `prefer` (header, optional, default `"return=minimal"`), `body: OrderCaptureRequest` (body, OPTIONAL), mock/metadata/auth-assertion headers optional.
+getOrder `Orders.GetOrderRequest`: `id` (path, required), `fields` (query, optional), mock/auth-assertion headers optional.
+
+### Models set/read (from `src/models/` files named by Type sources)
+
+- `OrderRequest` (`order-request.ts`): `intent: CheckoutPaymentIntent` required (`CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture = "CAPTURE"`), `purchaseUnits: PurchaseUnitRequest[]` required; `processingInstruction?`, `payer?`, `paymentSource?`, `applicationContext?` optional.
+- `PurchaseUnitRequest`: `amount: AmountWithBreakdown` required; `customId?`, `invoiceId?`, `items?: ItemRequest[]`, others optional. `AmountWithBreakdown`: `currencyCode: string` required, `value: string` required (decimal dollars string), `breakdown?: AmountBreakdown`; `AmountBreakdown.itemTotal?: Money`; `Money`: `currencyCode`+`value` required strings. `ItemRequest`: `name` required, `unitAmount: Money` required, `quantity: string` required, `sku?` optional.
+- `Order` (response, ALL members optional — assert the ones we use or treat as unknown): `id?`, `status?: OrderStatus` (`CREATED/SAVED/APPROVED/VOIDED/COMPLETED/PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED`), `purchaseUnits?: PurchaseUnit[]`. `PurchaseUnit.customId?`, `amount?`, `payments?: PaymentCollection`; `PaymentCollection.captures?: OrdersCapture[]`; `OrdersCapture`: `status?: CaptureStatus` (`COMPLETED/DECLINED/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED/PENDING/REFUNDED/FAILED`), `id?`, `amount?: Money`, `customId?`, `invoiceId?`. A truncated 2xx decodes silently with `undefined` members and a malformed 2xx rejects `DecodeError` (kind `"decode"`, not an ApiError) — both are "unknown", never "failed"/"absent".
+- `OrderCaptureRequest`: only `paymentSource?` — we send no body fields (body omitted entirely).
+
+### Webhook verification — NOT an SDK operation
+
+Verified in `sdk-map.md`: 5 resources / 40 operations, none for notifications/webhooks (client-initialization skill confirms generated SDKs have no webhook surface). Per checkout-hardening rule 6 this one call is made directly with `fetch` to `{PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature`, token from POST `{PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/oauth2/token` (client credentials, Basic), body exactly `{auth_algo, cert_url, transmission_id, transmission_sig, transmission_time}` from the `PAYPAL-*` headers + `webhook_id: PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` + `webhook_event` (parsed body). Act only on `verification_status:"SUCCESS"`, else 400 + no change. All Orders calls still go through the SDK.
+
+## 1b.1 DURABLE WRITES
+
+DUPLICATE CLAIMS
+
+| Write | Where the claim is stored | What rejects the second one | Where that rejection is caught | Where in the code |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| createOrder | shop `orders` row (status `pending`, method `paypal`) created BEFORE the SDK call; its id is sent as `PayPal-Request-Id` and as `purchase_units[0].custom_id`/`invoice_id` | orders row exists before the call; a retry of the same logical create reuses the same shop order id + same `PayPal-Request-Id` (provider dedupes on it); `orders.paypal_order_id` UNIQUE rejects binding one PayPal order to two shop orders | `catch` around the attach UPDATE in `POST /api/paypal/orders` handler, recognised by sqlite UNIQUE constraint (error code/message check, not message text alone where code available) | `server.js` `POST /api/paypal/orders` → `db.createOrder` then `lib/paypal.js#createOrder`, bind via `lib/db.js#attachPayPalOrder` |
+| captureOrder | `paypal_capture_claims` row, PK = shop order id (+ paypal order id), inserted BEFORE the SDK capture call | PK unique constraint on `paypal_capture_claims.order_id` refuses the second claim before it reaches PayPal | `catch`/boolean from `db.claimCapture` in the capture handler + service settle path; loser settles by reading the shop order and, if needed, `getOrder` from PayPal | `server.js` `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` → `lib/db.js#claimCapture`; tests `capture with a COMPLETED…` (claim seen inside faked fetch) and `two captures at once ship once` |
+| fulfil (paid transition) | `orders.status` itself | atomic `UPDATE orders SET status='paid',… WHERE id=? AND status='pending'` — only the caller seeing 1 changed row calls `fulfilOrder` | return value of `db.transitionToPaid` in the shared settle helper (capture route + webhook) | `server.js#settlePaid` → `lib/db.js#transitionToPaid`; tests `two captures at once…` and webhook replay test |
+
+Claim release: capture claim is released when PayPal *refuses* the capture (any `kind:"api"` error incl. INSTRUMENT_DECLINED / TRANSACTION_REFUSED) so the buyer can pick another instrument and retry; it is kept while outcome is unknown or paid.
+
+UNKNOWN OUTCOMES
+
+| Write | The operation you re-read with | The reference you search by | Where in the code | The test that fails the connection |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| captureOrder | `getOrder` | PayPal order id (path `id`), then match capture COMPLETED + amount/currency + purchase-unit `custom_id` = shop order | `lib/paypal.js#captureOrder` catch → `settleFromPayPal`/`getOrder`, validation in `evaluateOrder` | tests `unknown capture outcome is settled by re-reading the order from PayPal` (asserts the GET request was made) and `unknown capture outcome with nothing captured stays unknown, never failed`; never-sent counterpart: `a refused token (never sent) is a 502 and triggers no re-read` (asserts no GET) |
+| createOrder | none available in SDK (no search by `PayPal-Request-Id`/`custom_id`) — outcome reported unknown, shop order left `pending`, never "failed"; browser never receives a PayPal id so nothing can be captured against it | n/a | `lib/paypal.js#createOrder` (translated unknown propagates); `server.js` create handler leaves order `pending` when `err.unknown` | test `unknown create outcome leaves the shop order pending, never failed` (faked fetch throws on the create request) |
+
+Never-sent failures (kind `"auth"` = token refused, kind `"encode"` = nothing sent) get their own outcome (502 fixed message) and NO re-read — separate tests assert the re-read request was NOT made. Kinds `"connection"`/`"timeout"`/`"decode"` on capture → re-read above; found → settle from PayPal, not found or re-read fails → still unknown (502 "outcome unknown"), never failed.
+
+## 1b.2 CROSS-OPERATION INVARIANTS
+
+| Invariant | Where the legal set comes from | Enforced where | The test that proves it |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PayPal order id on capture/webhook-settle must be bound to a shop order this shop created | shop `orders` rows (`paypal_order_id` UNIQUE lookup) | capture route + webhook settle, BEFORE the capture claim and before any SDK write | capture with an unbound PayPal id → 404 and fake fetch shows no capture request |
+| `custom_id` on the PayPal purchase unit (and on the capture when present) must equal that shop order's id | the bound shop order row | shared capture validation used by capture route, getOrder settle and webhook | fake capture with wrong `custom_id` → unpaid, no shipment, capture SDK was called but fulfil was not |
+| Capture amount+currency must equal shop order total (cents → decimal string) + `USD` | shop order row `total_cents`/`currency` | same validation | fake COMPLETED capture for `0.01` → unpaid, no shipment |
+| Bag SKUs/quantities legal | `lib/catalog.js` via `priceCart` (known SKU, integer 1–10) | create-order route BEFORE creating the shop order / claim | bad qty/unknown SKU → 400, no shop order, no SDK call |
+
+## 1b.3 OPTIONAL REQUEST FIELDS
+
+createOrder:
+
+| Field | What requires it | Set it? |
+|---|---|---|
+| `body.intent` (required) | task: capture immediately | ✅ `"CAPTURE"` |
+| `body.purchaseUnits[].amount` (required) | task + hardening rules 1–2: server total, decimal string, `breakdown.item_total` = total | ✅ from `priceCart` via one `centsToPayPalAmount` fn |
+| `body.purchaseUnits[].customId`, `.invoiceId` | hardening rule 3 (bind PayPal order to shop order) | ✅ shop order id |
+| `body.purchaseUnits[].items[]` (`name`,`unitAmount`,`quantity` as string,`sku`) | hardening rule 2 item breakdown sums to total; sku from catalog line the task supplies | ✅ |
+| `payPalRequestId` | DUPLICATE CLAIMS row (create) | ✅ shop order id |
+| `prefer` | capture/read validation needs full `Order` (`purchase_units.payments.captures`), default `return=minimal` would hide it | ✅ `"return=representation"` |
+| `payPalMockResponse`, `payPalPartnerAttributionId`, `payPalClientMetadataId`, `payPalAuthAssertion`, `body.processingInstruction/payer/paymentSource/applicationContext`, PU `referenceId/payee/paymentInstruction/description/softDescriptor/shipping/supplementaryData` | nothing | ❌ leave out (never forward browser-supplied headers — mock-response injection attack) |
+
+captureOrder:
+
+| Field | What requires it | Set it? |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` (required) | task | ✅ PayPal order id from route |
+| `payPalRequestId` | DUPLICATE CLAIMS/UNKNOWN rows (stable reference per shop order capture) | ✅ shop order id |
+| `prefer` | need full capture details in response (as above) | ✅ `"return=representation"` |
+| `body` (`OrderCaptureRequest.paymentSource?`) | nothing | ❌ omit body entirely |
+| mock/metadata/auth-assertion headers | nothing | ❌ leave out |
+
+getOrder: only `id` ✅; `fields`, mock, auth-assertion ❌.
+
+Proof test: fake-fetch asserts the exact wire body keys and that `paypal-mock-response`/partner/metadata headers are absent (SDK's own `Idempotency-Key`/auth headers are the SDK's, not ours).
+
+## 1b.4 WHEN THE API SAYS NO (createOrder / captureOrder / getOrder — same ladder at the service boundary)
+
+| status | your app answers | the caller reads | test |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| a `4xx` other than 401/403/429 | the same `4xx` | PayPal's reason from `err.payload.body` (`message` + `details[].issue/description`); INSTRUMENT_DECLINED additionally tells buyer to choose another way to pay | fake 422 with reason; assert reason text in response, order unpaid |
+| 401 / 403 | 502 | fixed "PayPal is unavailable" (our credentials) | fake 401; assert 502 + fixed text, reason NOT leaked |
+| 429 | 503 | fixed "temporarily unavailable" (our quota) | — |
+| 5xx | 502 | fixed message | — |
+| no response, on a write (capture) | per UNKNOWN OUTCOMES (re-read via getOrder, else 502 unknown) | unknown — never "failed" | connection-failing fake asserts getOrder request made |
+| no response, on a read (getOrder settle) | 502 | fixed message / outcome unknown | — |
+| kind `auth`/`encode` (never sent) | 502 | fixed message; no re-read | token-401 fake asserts no getOrder request |
+
+Reasons are logged AND returned for caller-caused 4xx; SDK `err.message` (method+URL) is never put on the wire.
+
+## Routes & browser (per web-sdk-v6 + hardening skills)
+
+- `GET /api/paypal/config` → `{ clientId, scriptUrl, currency:"USD" }` + `testBuyerCountry` only in sandbox when `PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY` set. Secret never leaves server (rule 12).
+- `POST /api/paypal/orders` `{items, email?}` → prices server-side, creates shop order, SDK createOrder, stores PayPal id; returns `{ id: <PayPal order id>, orderId: <shop id> }` (browser `createOrder()` returns `{orderId: data.id}`).
+- `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` → claim, SDK capture, validate COMPLETED/amount/currency/custom_id, atomic paid transition, fulfil once. PENDING capture → 202 unpaid. Already fulfilled → 200 (safe re-entry, settles via getOrder when needed per rule 10 / ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED).
+- `POST /api/paypal/webhooks` → verify (rule 6), record event id once in `webhook_events` (PK; repeat → 200 no change, rule 7), act only: `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` → settle via getOrder + atomic fulfil; `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` and everything else → no state change (rules 4, 9). Never move a paid/fulfilled order backwards (rules 8–9 via the atomic `pending`-only transition).
+- Browser: script loaded once from config URL, `paypal.createInstance({clientId, components:["paypal-payments","venmo-payments","paypal-messages"], pageType:"checkout", ...(testBuyerCountry?{testBuyerCountry}:{})})`, `findEligibleMethods({currencyCode:"USD"})` gates hidden `<paypal-button>/<venmo-button>/<paypal-pay-later-button>` (Pay Later gets `productCode`/`countryCode` from `getDetails("paylater")`), one session per method, click handler starts `createOrder()` WITHOUT awaiting before `session.start({presentationMode:"auto"}, promise)`, `onApprove` posts capture, `onCancel`/`onError` pay nothing; `<paypal-message auto-bootstrap>` amount updated (decimal dollars string) on bag change; `sdk.createPayPalMessages()` after instance.
+
+## Assumptions & Blockers
+
+- Minor: shop currency is USD (catalog/`priceCart` returns `usd` → sent as `USD`).
+- Minor: webhook `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` resource identifies the order via `custom_id` and/or `supplementary_data.related_ids.order_id`; settle re-reads the order through the SDK before fulfilling, so a webhook body alone never fulfils.
+- Blocker-class fact resolved, not open: SDK has no webhook-verification operation → direct fetch per rule 6 (above). Create-order unknown outcome has no provider re-read → reported unknown (above).
+
+## REQUIRED READING
+
+| Step | Skill |
+|---|---|
+| Error boundary, kind ladder, arm handling | MUST load `typescript-error-handling` ✅ loaded |
+| Client construction, one long-lived client, base-URL override, logging off | MUST load `typescript-client-initialization` ✅ loaded |
+| OAuth2 credentials, missing-credential startup check | MUST load `typescript-authentication` ✅ loaded |
+| Flat request object, `.asApiResult()` not needed (throw-based with kind ladder) | MUST load `typescript-calling-endpoints` ✅ loaded |
+| Model required/optional, Money as string, enum members | MUST load `typescript-models` ✅ loaded |
+| Retry gate (POST not retried), fetch seam, no body logging | MUST load `typescript-configuration-resilience` ✅ loaded |
+| Fake `ClientOptions.fetch`, token request first, wire-shaped stubs, `maxRetries:0` in tests | MUST load `typescript-testing` ✅ loaded |
+
+No live PayPal calls during build (no credentials); tests use faked fetch only.
